1
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:03,647
Water...

2
00:00:04,857 --> 00:00:06,358
Earth...

3
00:00:06,818 --> 00:00:08,402
Fire...

4
00:00:08,945 --> 00:00:10,320
Air.

5
00:00:11,281 --> 00:00:14,616
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,451 --> 00:00:19,413
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,747 --> 00:00:22,666
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:23,959
could stop them.

9
00:00:24,043 --> 00:00:25,585
But when the world needed him most,

10
00:00:25,670 --> 00:00:26,920
he vanished.

11
00:00:27,422 --> 00:00:28,672
100 years passed,

12
00:00:28,756 --> 00:00:31,008
and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar--

13
00:00:31,092 --> 00:00:32,634
An airbender named Aang.

14
00:00:33,011 --> 00:00:35,012
And although
his airbending skills are great,

15
00:00:35,096 --> 00:00:37,723
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

16
00:00:37,807 --> 00:00:38,807
Oof!

17
00:00:39,183 --> 00:00:42,102
But I believe Aang can save the world.

18
00:01:04,792 --> 00:01:06,043
Would you sit down?!

19
00:01:06,127 --> 00:01:08,170
If we hit a bump,
you'll go flying off!

20
00:01:08,254 --> 00:01:09,504
What's bugging you anyway?

21
00:01:10,048 --> 00:01:11,590
It's what Avatar Roku said.

22
00:01:11,674 --> 00:01:13,508
I'm supposed to master
all four elements

23
00:01:13,593 --> 00:01:14,885
before that comet arrives.

24
00:01:14,969 --> 00:01:15,969
Well, let's see.

25
00:01:16,054 --> 00:01:17,554
You pretty much mastered airbending,

26
00:01:17,638 --> 00:01:19,431
and that only took you 112 years.

27
00:01:19,807 --> 00:01:20,807
I'm sure you can master

28
00:01:20,892 --> 00:01:22,184
three more elements by next summer.

29
00:01:22,935 --> 00:01:24,561
I haven't even started waterbending,

30
00:01:24,645 --> 00:01:26,730
and we're still weeks away
from the North Pole.

31
00:01:26,981 --> 00:01:28,482
What am I gonna do?!

32
00:01:28,566 --> 00:01:29,566
Calm down.

33
00:01:29,650 --> 00:01:30,776
It's gonna be ok.

34
00:01:31,486 --> 00:01:32,486
If you want,

35
00:01:32,570 --> 00:01:33,570
I can try and teach you

36
00:01:33,654 --> 00:01:34,654
some of the stuff I know.

37
00:01:34,739 --> 00:01:35,739
You'd do that?

38
00:01:36,407 --> 00:01:37,407
We'll need to find

39
00:01:37,492 --> 00:01:38,658
a good source of water first.

40
00:01:39,702 --> 00:01:41,620
Maybe we can find a puddle
for you to splash in.

41
00:01:44,707 --> 00:01:45,707
Nice puddle.

42
00:01:56,260 --> 00:01:57,386
Yeah!

43
00:01:57,470 --> 00:01:58,720
Don't start without me, boy!

44
00:01:58,805 --> 00:02:00,389
Remember the reason we're here.

45
00:02:00,473 --> 00:02:01,473
Right.

46
00:02:01,557 --> 00:02:02,849
Time to practice waterbending.

47
00:02:03,601 --> 00:02:05,560
Great. So, what am I supposed to do?

48
00:02:05,853 --> 00:02:07,396
You could clean the gunk

49
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:08,480
out of Appa's toes.

50
00:02:10,149 --> 00:02:12,192
So, while you guys
are playing in the water,

51
00:02:12,276 --> 00:02:13,527
I'm supposed to be hard at work

52
00:02:13,611 --> 00:02:15,612
picking mud
out of a giant bison's feet?

53
00:02:15,863 --> 00:02:16,863
Mud and bugs.

54
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:20,200
Ok.

55
00:02:29,168 --> 00:02:30,419
Whoa! Whoa!

56
00:02:30,503 --> 00:02:31,711
Oof!

57
00:02:31,796 --> 00:02:32,879
Someone's changing our course.

58
00:02:35,925 --> 00:02:37,175
What's the meaning of this mutiny?

59
00:02:37,260 --> 00:02:38,885
No one told you to change course.

60
00:02:39,345 --> 00:02:41,012
Actually, someone did.

61
00:02:41,431 --> 00:02:42,431
I assure you,

62
00:02:42,515 --> 00:02:44,891
it is a matter of utmost importance,

63
00:02:44,976 --> 00:02:46,059
Prince Zuko.

64
00:02:46,602 --> 00:02:47,894
Is it something to do with the Avatar?

65
00:02:48,438 --> 00:02:49,855
Even more urgent.

66
00:02:49,939 --> 00:02:51,148
It seems I--

67
00:02:51,232 --> 00:02:52,941
I've lost my lotus tile.

68
00:02:54,485 --> 00:02:55,610
Lotus tile?

69
00:02:55,903 --> 00:02:57,737
For my pai sho game.

70
00:02:57,822 --> 00:02:59,614
Most people think the lotus tile

71
00:02:59,699 --> 00:03:00,824
insignificant.

72
00:03:01,367 --> 00:03:04,703
But it is essential
for the unusual strategy

73
00:03:04,787 --> 00:03:06,538
that I employ.

74
00:03:06,622 --> 00:03:09,624
You've changed our course
for a stupid lotus tile?

75
00:03:09,709 --> 00:03:11,585
See, you, like most people,

76
00:03:11,669 --> 00:03:13,670
underestimate its value.

77
00:03:13,921 --> 00:03:16,089
Just give me 10 minutes
to check the merchants

78
00:03:16,174 --> 00:03:17,507
at this port of call.

79
00:03:17,592 --> 00:03:20,760
Hopefully, they'll have
the lotus tile in stock

80
00:03:20,845 --> 00:03:23,305
and I can get on with my life.

81
00:03:26,184 --> 00:03:29,227
I'm lucky to have such
an understanding nephew.

82
00:03:32,940 --> 00:03:34,065
Yeah, don't get too happy.

83
00:03:34,150 --> 00:03:35,192
You've got to do me next.

84
00:03:37,528 --> 00:03:38,862
This is a pretty basic move,

85
00:03:38,946 --> 00:03:41,031
but it still took me
months to perfect.

86
00:03:41,491 --> 00:03:42,782
So, don't be frustrated

87
00:03:42,867 --> 00:03:44,159
if you don't get it right away.

88
00:03:45,161 --> 00:03:47,829
Just push and pull the water
like this.

89
00:03:47,914 --> 00:03:49,873
The key is getting
the wrist movement right.

90
00:03:51,417 --> 00:03:52,417
Like this?

91
00:03:55,254 --> 00:03:56,588
That's almost right.

92
00:03:57,048 --> 00:03:58,131
If you keep practicing,

93
00:03:58,216 --> 00:03:59,341
I'm sure eventually--

94
00:03:59,425 --> 00:04:00,842
Hey, I'm bending it already!

95
00:04:01,219 --> 00:04:03,553
Wow! I can't believe
you got that so quickly.

96
00:04:04,180 --> 00:04:06,264
It took me two months
to learn that move.

97
00:04:06,349 --> 00:04:07,516
Well, you had to figure it out

98
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:08,767
all on your own.

99
00:04:08,851 --> 00:04:10,477
I'm lucky enough
to have a great teacher.

100
00:04:10,978 --> 00:04:11,978
Thanks.

101
00:04:12,438 --> 00:04:13,647
So, what's next?

102
00:04:13,731 --> 00:04:15,357
This is a more difficult move.

103
00:04:15,441 --> 00:04:17,317
I call it streaming the water.

104
00:04:20,696 --> 00:04:21,863
It's harder than it looks,

105
00:04:21,948 --> 00:04:23,073
so don't be disappointed if...

106
00:04:34,043 --> 00:04:35,085
Nice work.

107
00:04:35,169 --> 00:04:37,420
Though the over-the-head
flair was unnecessary.

108
00:04:38,047 --> 00:04:39,047
Sorry.

109
00:04:39,131 --> 00:04:40,507
Well, don't stop now.

110
00:04:40,591 --> 00:04:41,758
Keep 'em coming.

111
00:04:41,842 --> 00:04:43,510
Well, I kind of know
this one other move,

112
00:04:43,970 --> 00:04:45,220
But it's pretty hard.

113
00:04:45,304 --> 00:04:46,972
I haven't even totally
figured it out yet.

114
00:04:47,431 --> 00:04:50,684
The idea is to create
a big, powerful wave.

115
00:04:56,274 --> 00:04:57,440
So, like this?

116
00:05:02,780 --> 00:05:03,780
Aang!

117
00:05:12,081 --> 00:05:13,665
Looks like I got
the hang of that move.

118
00:05:13,749 --> 00:05:15,000
What else you got?

119
00:05:15,084 --> 00:05:16,710
That's enough practicing for today.

120
00:05:17,086 --> 00:05:18,420
Yeah, I'll say!

121
00:05:18,504 --> 00:05:20,005
You just practiced our supplies

122
00:05:20,089 --> 00:05:21,089
Down the river.

123
00:05:21,173 --> 00:05:22,924
Sorry.

124
00:05:23,259 --> 00:05:24,759
I'm sure we can find some way

125
00:05:24,844 --> 00:05:25,844
to replace all this stuff.

126
00:05:26,095 --> 00:05:27,220
My life was hard enough

127
00:05:27,305 --> 00:05:28,388
when you were just an airbender.

128
00:05:39,275 --> 00:05:40,900
Please, put me down!

129
00:05:40,985 --> 00:05:42,944
See the wonder in this bag!

130
00:05:43,487 --> 00:05:46,114
Who's brave enough
to look into this bag?!

131
00:05:46,198 --> 00:05:47,198
Wow!

132
00:05:50,202 --> 00:05:52,245
We've got exactly
three copper pieces left

133
00:05:52,330 --> 00:05:53,663
from the money that King Bumi gave us.

134
00:05:53,748 --> 00:05:55,123
Let's spend it wisely.

135
00:05:55,374 --> 00:05:57,667
Make that
two copper pieces, Sokka.

136
00:05:58,085 --> 00:05:59,461
I couldn't say no to this whistle.

137
00:06:03,424 --> 00:06:04,591
It doesn't even work.

138
00:06:07,637 --> 00:06:10,055
See? Even Momo thinks
it's a piece of junk.

139
00:06:10,514 --> 00:06:11,765
No offense, Aang,

140
00:06:11,849 --> 00:06:13,516
but I'll hold the money from now on.

141
00:06:18,939 --> 00:06:21,149
Earth Nation! Fire Nation!

142
00:06:21,233 --> 00:06:22,484
Water Nation.

143
00:06:22,568 --> 00:06:25,153
So long as bargains
are your inclination,

144
00:06:25,237 --> 00:06:26,780
you're welcome here!

145
00:06:26,864 --> 00:06:27,947
Don't be shy.

146
00:06:28,032 --> 00:06:29,741
Come on by!

147
00:06:30,076 --> 00:06:31,493
You there!

148
00:06:31,577 --> 00:06:33,536
I can see from your clothing

149
00:06:33,621 --> 00:06:35,497
that you're world traveling types.

150
00:06:35,581 --> 00:06:37,082
Perhaps I can interest you

151
00:06:37,166 --> 00:06:39,209
in some exotic curios?

152
00:06:39,502 --> 00:06:40,585
Sure!

153
00:06:40,670 --> 00:06:41,836
What are curios?

154
00:06:44,215 --> 00:06:46,007
I'm not entirely sure,

155
00:06:46,092 --> 00:06:47,217
But we got 'em.

156
00:07:03,192 --> 00:07:07,362
I've never seen
such a fine specimen of lemur.

157
00:07:07,738 --> 00:07:09,781
That beast would fetch me a hefty sum

158
00:07:09,865 --> 00:07:11,866
if you'd be interested in bartering.

159
00:07:15,621 --> 00:07:16,621
Momo's not for sale.

160
00:07:26,173 --> 00:07:27,465
Look at this, Aang!

161
00:07:27,550 --> 00:07:29,509
It's a waterbending scroll.

162
00:07:29,927 --> 00:07:31,636
Check out these crazy moves.

163
00:07:32,138 --> 00:07:34,556
Where did you get
a waterbending scroll?

164
00:07:35,182 --> 00:07:37,642
Let's just say I got it up north

165
00:07:37,727 --> 00:07:39,477
at a most reasonable price--

166
00:07:39,854 --> 00:07:40,854
Free.

167
00:07:43,858 --> 00:07:45,442
Wait a minute.

168
00:07:45,526 --> 00:07:46,985
Sea-loving traders

169
00:07:47,069 --> 00:07:49,446
with suspiciously acquired merchandise

170
00:07:50,114 --> 00:07:52,240
and pet reptile birds?

171
00:07:52,658 --> 00:07:54,159
You guys are pirates!

172
00:07:54,660 --> 00:07:56,494
We prefer to think of ourselves as

173
00:07:56,579 --> 00:07:57,996
high-risk traders.

174
00:07:59,623 --> 00:08:02,292
So, how much for the traded scroll?

175
00:08:02,668 --> 00:08:03,918
I've already got a buyer--

176
00:08:04,003 --> 00:08:05,920
A nobleman in the Earth Kingdom--

177
00:08:06,338 --> 00:08:08,673
Unless, of course, you kids have

178
00:08:08,758 --> 00:08:11,634
200 gold pieces on you right now.

179
00:08:11,719 --> 00:08:13,511
I know how to deal
with these guys, Katara.

180
00:08:13,888 --> 00:08:14,888
Pirates love to haggle.

181
00:08:17,433 --> 00:08:19,267
Watch and learn.

182
00:08:19,977 --> 00:08:22,479
What say ye to the price of...

183
00:08:22,563 --> 00:08:24,022
One copper piece?

184
00:08:24,940 --> 00:08:26,649
Ha ha ha ha!

185
00:08:26,734 --> 00:08:29,277
The price is 200 gold pieces.

186
00:08:29,653 --> 00:08:31,946
I don't haggle on items this rare.

187
00:08:32,198 --> 00:08:34,741
Ok, two copper pieces.

188
00:08:35,284 --> 00:08:37,619
It's not as amusing
the second time, boy.

189
00:08:37,870 --> 00:08:39,662
Aang, can we get out of here?

190
00:08:39,747 --> 00:08:41,414
I feel like we're getting weird looks.

191
00:08:41,874 --> 00:08:44,292
Aye! We be casting off now!

192
00:08:45,002 --> 00:08:46,711
What was that all about, Katara?

193
00:08:46,796 --> 00:08:48,630
Yeah, I was just starting
to browse through

194
00:08:48,714 --> 00:08:49,798
their boomerang collection.

195
00:08:50,299 --> 00:08:51,466
I'll just feel a lot better

196
00:08:51,550 --> 00:08:52,592
once we get away from here.

197
00:08:53,135 --> 00:08:54,219
Hey, you!

198
00:08:54,303 --> 00:08:55,553
Get back here!

199
00:08:55,638 --> 00:08:56,679
Well, well.

200
00:08:56,764 --> 00:08:58,306
Look who's come to their senses.

201
00:08:58,808 --> 00:09:00,141
Told you the haggling would pay off.

202
00:09:12,029 --> 00:09:13,196
There they are!

203
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:14,280
Get 'em!

204
00:09:14,365 --> 00:09:16,324
Nobody's going nowhere!

205
00:09:19,370 --> 00:09:21,037
I don't think these pirates

206
00:09:21,121 --> 00:09:22,330
are here to trade with us.

207
00:09:22,414 --> 00:09:23,957
Get back here!

208
00:09:24,041 --> 00:09:25,667
You little--

209
00:09:25,751 --> 00:09:26,793
Come on!

210
00:09:27,127 --> 00:09:28,127
This way.

211
00:09:28,212 --> 00:09:29,295
Let's cut 'em off!

212
00:09:31,423 --> 00:09:36,135
Whoa!

213
00:09:36,220 --> 00:09:37,220
Oof!

214
00:09:51,110 --> 00:09:52,485
My cabbages!

215
00:09:52,570 --> 00:09:54,195
This place is worse than Omashu!

216
00:10:01,328 --> 00:10:02,328
Aha!

217
00:10:05,624 --> 00:10:06,833
I hope that lemur of yours

218
00:10:06,917 --> 00:10:08,167
has nine lives.

219
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:13,298
Now, who gets to taste

220
00:10:13,382 --> 00:10:15,425
the steel of my blade first?

221
00:10:15,509 --> 00:10:16,759
No, thanks.

222
00:10:17,511 --> 00:10:18,511
Haa!

223
00:10:20,848 --> 00:10:22,140
Grab on tight!

224
00:10:22,224 --> 00:10:23,600
Aang, I thought we were

225
00:10:23,684 --> 00:10:25,143
running away from the pirates.

226
00:10:25,561 --> 00:10:26,811
Just hang on.

227
00:10:26,896 --> 00:10:27,979
Whoa!

228
00:10:29,773 --> 00:10:31,232
Whoa!

229
00:10:34,695 --> 00:10:36,487
I used to kind of look up to pirates,

230
00:10:36,572 --> 00:10:37,989
but those guys are terrible.

231
00:10:38,073 --> 00:10:39,157
I know.

232
00:10:39,241 --> 00:10:41,200
That's why I took this.

233
00:10:41,619 --> 00:10:42,619
No way!

234
00:10:42,703 --> 00:10:44,037
Isn't it great?!

235
00:10:44,121 --> 00:10:45,830
No wonder they were
trying to hack us up.

236
00:10:46,165 --> 00:10:48,124
You stole their waterbending scroll.

237
00:10:48,208 --> 00:10:49,876
I prefer to think of it as

238
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:51,586
high-risk trading.

239
00:10:51,670 --> 00:10:52,670
Ha ha ha.

240
00:10:52,755 --> 00:10:54,213
Good one, Katara.

241
00:10:54,298 --> 00:10:56,299
Sokka, where to you think they got it?

242
00:10:56,592 --> 00:10:58,593
They stole it from a waterbender.

243
00:10:59,053 --> 00:11:00,136
It doesn't matter.

244
00:11:00,220 --> 00:11:01,679
You put all of our lives in danger

245
00:11:01,764 --> 00:11:02,764
just so you could learn

246
00:11:02,848 --> 00:11:04,515
some stupid, fancy splashes.

247
00:11:04,934 --> 00:11:07,602
These are real waterbending forms.

248
00:11:07,686 --> 00:11:08,895
You know how crucial it is

249
00:11:08,979 --> 00:11:10,563
for Aang to learn waterbending.

250
00:11:12,191 --> 00:11:13,399
Whatever.

251
00:11:13,484 --> 00:11:14,776
Well, what's done is done.

252
00:11:14,860 --> 00:11:15,944
We have it.

253
00:11:16,028 --> 00:11:17,236
We might as well learn from it.

254
00:11:26,163 --> 00:11:28,748
I've checked all the shops
on this pier.

255
00:11:28,832 --> 00:11:32,377
Not a lotus tile
in the entire marketplace.

256
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:33,920
It's good to know this trip

257
00:11:34,004 --> 00:11:35,004
was a complete waste of time

258
00:11:35,089 --> 00:11:36,381
for everyone!

259
00:11:36,465 --> 00:11:37,840
Quite the contrary.

260
00:11:38,467 --> 00:11:40,802
I always say
the only thing better than

261
00:11:40,886 --> 00:11:43,096
finding something you are looking for

262
00:11:43,681 --> 00:11:46,557
is finding something
you weren't looking for

263
00:11:46,642 --> 00:11:48,935
at a great bargain.

264
00:11:49,979 --> 00:11:51,646
You bought a sungi horn?

265
00:11:51,730 --> 00:11:53,231
For music night on the ship.

266
00:11:53,691 --> 00:11:55,817
Now, if we only had some woodwinds.

267
00:11:57,820 --> 00:11:59,862
This place looks promising.

268
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:03,574
That is handsome!

269
00:12:03,951 --> 00:12:06,327
Wouldn't it look
magnificent in the galley?

270
00:12:06,412 --> 00:12:07,912
We lost the water tribe girl

271
00:12:07,997 --> 00:12:08,997
and the little bald monk

272
00:12:09,081 --> 00:12:10,581
she was traveling with.

273
00:12:10,666 --> 00:12:12,625
This monk, did he have
an arrow on his head?

274
00:12:15,254 --> 00:12:16,921
I just want to try
this one move first,

275
00:12:17,006 --> 00:12:18,214
and then it's all yours.

276
00:12:18,298 --> 00:12:19,298
Here, hold it open for me.

277
00:12:23,178 --> 00:12:24,554
The single water whip.

278
00:12:25,014 --> 00:12:26,431
Looks doable.

279
00:12:32,604 --> 00:12:33,604
Ha ha ha!

280
00:12:33,689 --> 00:12:35,023
What's so funny?

281
00:12:35,107 --> 00:12:36,816
I'm sorry, but you deserved that.

282
00:12:36,900 --> 00:12:38,109
You've been duped.

283
00:12:38,193 --> 00:12:39,861
She's only interested
in teaching herself.

284
00:12:39,945 --> 00:12:41,279
Aang will get his turn

285
00:12:41,363 --> 00:12:42,697
once I figure out the water whip.

286
00:12:47,745 --> 00:12:49,912
Why can't I get
this stupid move?!

287
00:12:49,997 --> 00:12:50,997
You'll get it.

288
00:12:53,667 --> 00:12:55,126
You've just gotta shift your weight

289
00:12:55,210 --> 00:12:56,461
through the stances.

290
00:12:57,004 --> 00:12:58,129
There. See?

291
00:12:58,213 --> 00:12:59,213
The key to bending is--

292
00:12:59,298 --> 00:13:01,174
Will you please shut your air hole!

293
00:13:01,258 --> 00:13:02,884
Believe it or not,
your infinite wisdom

294
00:13:02,968 --> 00:13:04,552
gets a little old sometimes!

295
00:13:05,012 --> 00:13:06,637
Why don't we just
throw the scroll away

296
00:13:06,722 --> 00:13:09,265
since you're so naturally gifted?!

297
00:13:10,893 --> 00:13:11,893
What?!

298
00:13:14,772 --> 00:13:16,481
My gosh, Aang.

299
00:13:16,565 --> 00:13:18,274
I am so sorry.

300
00:13:18,734 --> 00:13:20,276
I don't know what came over me.

301
00:13:20,778 --> 00:13:21,903
But you know what?

302
00:13:21,987 --> 00:13:23,362
It won't happen again.

303
00:13:23,739 --> 00:13:25,031
Here, this is yours.

304
00:13:25,282 --> 00:13:26,282
I don't want to have

305
00:13:26,366 --> 00:13:27,784
anything to do with it anymore.

306
00:13:28,243 --> 00:13:29,285
It's ok, Katara.

307
00:13:29,578 --> 00:13:30,620
What about Momo?

308
00:13:30,704 --> 00:13:32,080
He's the real victim here.

309
00:13:32,164 --> 00:13:33,289
I'm sorry, Momo.

310
00:13:33,540 --> 00:13:34,749
And what about me?

311
00:13:34,833 --> 00:13:35,833
There was that time you--

312
00:13:35,918 --> 00:13:37,043
No more apologies.

313
00:13:48,847 --> 00:13:50,681
Shouldn't we stop to search the woods?

314
00:13:50,891 --> 00:13:52,058
We don't need to stop.

315
00:13:52,142 --> 00:13:53,768
They stole
a waterbending scroll, right?

316
00:13:55,354 --> 00:13:56,729
Then they'll be on the water.

317
00:14:17,501 --> 00:14:18,543
Shh.

318
00:14:18,627 --> 00:14:20,837
Momo, go back to sleep.

319
00:14:23,757 --> 00:14:24,757
Shh!

320
00:14:35,853 --> 00:14:36,894
Shoot!

321
00:14:36,979 --> 00:14:39,272
Come on, water! Work with me here!

322
00:14:39,898 --> 00:14:41,524
Ok, what if I-- Ow!

323
00:14:44,111 --> 00:14:45,153
Ok, Katara,

324
00:14:45,237 --> 00:14:47,155
shift your weight through the stances.

325
00:14:54,621 --> 00:14:56,539
No!

326
00:14:56,623 --> 00:14:57,623
Let go of me!

327
00:15:00,210 --> 00:15:01,878
I'll save you from the pirates.

328
00:15:10,554 --> 00:15:11,846
Tell me where he is,

329
00:15:11,930 --> 00:15:13,264
and I won't hurt you or your brother.

330
00:15:13,348 --> 00:15:14,348
Go jump in the river!

331
00:15:16,310 --> 00:15:17,727
Try to understand,

332
00:15:17,811 --> 00:15:18,936
I need to capture him

333
00:15:19,021 --> 00:15:20,188
to restore something I've lost--

334
00:15:20,606 --> 00:15:21,731
My honor.

335
00:15:22,399 --> 00:15:23,566
Perhaps in exchange,

336
00:15:23,650 --> 00:15:24,859
I can restore something you've lost.

337
00:15:27,362 --> 00:15:28,946
My mother's necklace.

338
00:15:29,865 --> 00:15:30,948
How did you get that?!

339
00:15:31,283 --> 00:15:32,283
I didn't steal it

340
00:15:32,367 --> 00:15:33,451
if that's what you're wondering.

341
00:15:33,911 --> 00:15:35,661
Tell me where he is.

342
00:15:35,746 --> 00:15:36,746
No!

343
00:15:36,830 --> 00:15:38,664
Enough of this necklace garbage.

344
00:15:39,041 --> 00:15:41,125
You promised the scroll.

345
00:15:41,835 --> 00:15:43,753
I wonder how much money this is worth.

346
00:15:43,837 --> 00:15:45,129
No!

347
00:15:45,714 --> 00:15:46,881
A lot, apparently.

348
00:15:47,507 --> 00:15:49,592
Now, you help me find what I want,

349
00:15:49,676 --> 00:15:50,801
you'll get this back,

350
00:15:50,886 --> 00:15:52,637
and everyone goes home happy.

351
00:15:53,180 --> 00:15:55,264
Search the woods for the boy
and meet back here.

352
00:15:55,349 --> 00:15:56,349
Fine.

353
00:16:02,564 --> 00:16:03,689
Where did she go?

354
00:16:04,066 --> 00:16:05,149
I don't believe it.

355
00:16:06,318 --> 00:16:07,318
What's wrong?

356
00:16:07,402 --> 00:16:08,444
She took the scroll.

357
00:16:08,528 --> 00:16:09,779
She's obsessed with that thing.

358
00:16:09,863 --> 00:16:11,155
It's just a matter of time

359
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:12,323
before she gets us all in deep--

360
00:16:12,407 --> 00:16:13,658
Whoa!

361
00:16:26,463 --> 00:16:27,755
I've got him. Come on!

362
00:16:28,215 --> 00:16:30,925
What?
I'm not good enough to kidnap?

363
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:32,343
Aagh!

364
00:16:36,098 --> 00:16:37,223
Nice work.

365
00:16:43,605 --> 00:16:45,106
Aang, this is all my fault.

366
00:16:45,649 --> 00:16:46,816
No, Katara, it isn't.

367
00:16:47,025 --> 00:16:48,442
Yeah, it kind of is.

368
00:16:49,861 --> 00:16:51,112
Give me the boy.

369
00:16:51,280 --> 00:16:53,447
You give us the scroll.

370
00:16:53,949 --> 00:16:55,783
You're really gonna
hand over the Avatar

371
00:16:55,867 --> 00:16:57,827
for a stupid piece of parchment?

372
00:16:57,911 --> 00:16:59,078
Don't listen to him.

373
00:16:59,162 --> 00:17:00,705
He's trying to turn
us against each other.

374
00:17:01,331 --> 00:17:03,291
Your friend is the Avatar?

375
00:17:03,375 --> 00:17:04,417
Sure is.

376
00:17:04,501 --> 00:17:06,210
And I'll bet he'll fetch a lot more

377
00:17:06,295 --> 00:17:08,129
on the black market
than that fancy scroll.

378
00:17:08,630 --> 00:17:09,797
Shut your mouth,

379
00:17:09,881 --> 00:17:11,048
you water tribe peasant!

380
00:17:11,466 --> 00:17:14,260
Yeah, Sokka,
you really should shut your mouth.

381
00:17:14,720 --> 00:17:15,970
I'm just saying,

382
00:17:16,054 --> 00:17:17,388
it's bad business sense.

383
00:17:17,472 --> 00:17:18,764
Just imagine how much the Fire Lord

384
00:17:18,849 --> 00:17:20,308
would pay for the Avatar.

385
00:17:20,559 --> 00:17:22,518
You guys would be set for life.

386
00:17:22,936 --> 00:17:24,437
Keep the scroll.

387
00:17:24,521 --> 00:17:26,230
We can buy 100 with the reward

388
00:17:26,315 --> 00:17:27,523
we'll get for the kid.

389
00:17:28,025 --> 00:17:30,401
You'll regret breaking a deal with me.

390
00:17:52,632 --> 00:17:53,674
Thanks, Momo.

391
00:17:53,759 --> 00:17:55,343
I owe you a bushel of apples.

392
00:18:22,120 --> 00:18:23,120
Hey!

393
00:18:35,675 --> 00:18:36,675
Aah!

394
00:18:37,094 --> 00:18:39,136
Aang, are you there?

395
00:18:39,221 --> 00:18:41,347
I'm over here! Follow my voice.

396
00:18:41,681 --> 00:18:43,432
Where? I can't find you!

397
00:18:43,517 --> 00:18:44,642
I'm right here!

398
00:18:49,398 --> 00:18:50,689
Never mind.

399
00:18:50,941 --> 00:18:51,982
I'll find you!

400
00:18:53,276 --> 00:18:54,777
Run!

401
00:18:56,613 --> 00:18:58,155
Katara, you're ok.

402
00:18:58,532 --> 00:18:59,949
Help me get this boat
back in the water

403
00:19:00,033 --> 00:19:01,158
so we can get out of here.

404
00:19:05,539 --> 00:19:06,831
We need a team of rhinos

405
00:19:06,915 --> 00:19:08,040
to budge this ship.

406
00:19:08,125 --> 00:19:09,375
A team of rhinos...

407
00:19:09,459 --> 00:19:11,293
Or two waterbenders.

408
00:19:22,139 --> 00:19:23,305
Everybody in!

409
00:19:26,643 --> 00:19:28,144
Are you so busy fighting

410
00:19:28,228 --> 00:19:29,812
you cannot see your own ship

411
00:19:29,896 --> 00:19:31,522
has set sail?

412
00:19:31,606 --> 00:19:33,441
We have no time
for your proverbs, uncle.

413
00:19:33,942 --> 00:19:35,192
It's no proverb.

414
00:19:36,903 --> 00:19:38,362
Bleeding hog monkeys!

415
00:19:39,114 --> 00:19:40,531
Ha ha ha ha!

416
00:19:45,078 --> 00:19:47,371
Hey, that's my boat!

417
00:19:47,456 --> 00:19:49,498
Maybe it should be a proverb.

418
00:19:49,583 --> 00:19:50,583
Come on, uncle.

419
00:19:54,171 --> 00:19:56,338
Sokka, can't you make it
go any faster?

420
00:19:56,631 --> 00:19:58,007
I don't know how.

421
00:19:58,091 --> 00:19:59,717
This thing wasn't made
by the water tribe.

422
00:20:07,058 --> 00:20:11,312
Whoa!

423
00:20:15,984 --> 00:20:17,026
Oof!

424
00:20:17,527 --> 00:20:19,153
Hey! You did the water whip.

425
00:20:19,488 --> 00:20:21,030
I couldn't have done it
without your help.

426
00:20:21,364 --> 00:20:23,032
Will you two quit
congratulating each other

427
00:20:23,116 --> 00:20:24,158
and help me out?

428
00:20:41,051 --> 00:20:42,301
That's good.

429
00:20:43,011 --> 00:20:44,220
Wah!

430
00:20:44,304 --> 00:20:45,387
Hah!

431
00:20:51,770 --> 00:20:53,062
Aang, look!

432
00:20:56,024 --> 00:20:57,483
No!

433
00:21:05,116 --> 00:21:06,951
Aah!!

434
00:21:07,035 --> 00:21:08,494
Have you lost your mind?

435
00:21:08,578 --> 00:21:10,704
This is no time for flute practice!

436
00:21:12,666 --> 00:21:13,832
We can stop the boat.

437
00:21:13,917 --> 00:21:15,167
Aang, together,

438
00:21:15,252 --> 00:21:16,377
push and pull the water.

439
00:21:24,052 --> 00:21:25,135
It's working.

440
00:21:25,220 --> 00:21:26,220
It's slowing down.

441
00:21:33,728 --> 00:21:34,853
We're doing it!

442
00:21:34,938 --> 00:21:36,272
But we have another problem.

443
00:21:38,733 --> 00:21:40,025
Whoa! Whoa!

444
00:21:41,945 --> 00:21:43,153
Jump!

445
00:21:58,712 --> 00:22:01,130
I knew a bison whistle
would come in handy.

446
00:22:01,464 --> 00:22:02,548
Thanks, Appa.

447
00:22:02,632 --> 00:22:04,008
Yeah, we owe you one.

448
00:22:07,679 --> 00:22:08,721
My boat!

449
00:22:14,728 --> 00:22:15,811
Prince Zuko,

450
00:22:15,895 --> 00:22:17,896
you're really going to
get a kick out of this.

451
00:22:18,773 --> 00:22:22,651
That lotus tile
was in my sleeve the whole time!

452
00:22:31,620 --> 00:22:32,703
Aang,

453
00:22:32,787 --> 00:22:34,330
I still owe you an apology.

454
00:22:35,165 --> 00:22:36,749
You were just so good at waterbending

455
00:22:36,833 --> 00:22:38,208
without really trying.

456
00:22:38,293 --> 00:22:39,710
I got so competitive

457
00:22:39,794 --> 00:22:41,086
that I put us all in danger.

458
00:22:41,713 --> 00:22:42,838
I'm sorry.

459
00:22:43,298 --> 00:22:44,757
That's ok, Katara.

460
00:22:44,841 --> 00:22:47,801
Besides, who needs
that stupid scroll anyway?

461
00:22:47,886 --> 00:22:50,095
Is that really how you feel?

462
00:22:50,180 --> 00:22:51,305
The scroll!

463
00:22:51,389 --> 00:22:53,140
First, what did you learn?

464
00:22:53,558 --> 00:22:54,767
Stealing is wrong.

465
00:22:56,645 --> 00:22:57,978
Unless it's from pirates.

466
00:22:58,355 --> 00:22:59,438
Ha ha ha!

467
00:22:59,522 --> 00:23:00,648
Good one, Katara.
